---
// The create pipeline figure: the portrait layout of the socials diagram
// (source: diagrams/social-flow.html, `post` variant, rendered by
// scripts/render-diagram.mjs into public/blog/). One PNG per theme; the pair
// swaps on the OS preference and on the site's own toggle, which stamps
// data-theme on the root. Portrait so the stage text stays near its designed
// size inside the prose column instead of breaking out of it; each image
// links to the full-size file.
---

<figure class="pipeline">
  <a class="light" href="/blog/create-pipeline-light.png" target="_blank">
    <img
      src="/blog/create-pipeline-light.png"
      width="800"
      height="1550"
      loading="lazy"
      alt="The copperhead create pipeline: brief.md in, eight gated stages from spec to dev plan along a snaking copper trace, a design package out."
    />
  </a>
  <a class="dark" href="/blog/create-pipeline-dark.png" target="_blank">
    <img
      src="/blog/create-pipeline-dark.png"
      width="800"
      height="1550"
      loading="lazy"
      alt="The copperhead create pipeline: brief.md in, eight gated stages from spec to dev plan along a snaking copper trace, a design package out."
    />
  </a>
</figure>

<style>
  .pipeline {
    /* 680 against the 800px render: type lands at 0.85 of designed size,
       comfortably legible, without the figure towering over the column */
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 2.4rem auto;
  }

  .pipeline img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  /* theme pairing: the dark render on the dark page, in both the OS-preference
     and explicit-toggle paths */
  .dark {
    display: none;
  }

  :global(:root[data-theme='dark']) .light {
    display: none;
  }

  :global(:root[data-theme='dark']) .dark {
    display: block;
  }

  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :global(:root:not([data-theme='light'])) .light {
      display: none;
    }

    :global(:root:not([data-theme='light'])) .dark {
      display: block;
    }
  }
</style>
